  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Law enforcement monitoring and human-elephant conflict mitigation in Kaeng Krachan National Park, Thailand - Year 11</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to secure the long-term conservation of the wild elephant population and its habitat in Kaeng Krachan National Park by increasing the effectiveness of protection efforts and reducing human-elephant conflict (HEC) in the region. Project activities will include: 1) support of law enforcement monitoring using SMART software by providing training to guard teams, and field equipment, rations, and supplies for foot patrols; 2) reduction of HEC by promoting and monitoring standard HEC mitigation methods in local and extension of the semi-permanent fence in Huai Sad Yai; and 3) expansion of elephant conservation education directed at villagers from four HEC target sites, follow-up activities with three secondary schools, and an education campaign for tourists. This project will lead to more effective patrolling and law enforcement activities in the Park, better provisioned, trained, and motivated staff who are capable of addressing the threat of elephant poaching gangs, and reduced retaliatory elephant deaths.</narrative>
  </description>
